{"slug":"mariannette-miller-meeks","qid":"Q58495662","name":"Mariannette Miller-Meeks","desc":"American physician and politician (born 1955)","article":"Mariannette Miller-Meeks","born":"1955-09-06","died":null,"birthplace":"Herlong","parties":["Republican Party of Iowa"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"IA-01","f":2023,"u":null},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"IA-02","f":2021,"u":2023},{"t":"Iowa Senate","w":"","f":2019,"u":2021}],"summary":"Mariannette Jane Miller-Meeks (née Miller; born September 6, 1955) is an American physician and politician who has served as a U.S. representative from Iowa since 2021. Her district, numbered the 2nd from 2021 to 2023 and the 1st since 2023, includes most of Iowa's southeastern quadrant, including Davenport, Bettendorf, Burlington, and Iowa City. Previously, Miller-Meeks served in the Iowa Senate from 2019 to 2021.","photo":{"f":"mariannette-miller-meeks.jpg","by":"House Creative Services","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariannette_Miller-Meeks_117th_U.S_Congress.jpg"},"history":[{"y":2026,"o":"H","k":"IA-01","p":"R","n":"Mariannette Miller-Meeks","race":"IA-01"},{"y":2024,"o":"H","k":"IA-01","p":"R","v":206955,"s":49.98,"w":true,"n":"Mariannette Miller-Meeks"},{"y":2022,"o":"H","k":"IA-01","p":"R","v":162947,"s":53.36,"w":true,"n":"Mariannette Miller-Meeks"},{"y":2020,"o":"H","k":"IA-02","p":"R","v":196964,"s":49.91,"w":true,"n":"Mariannette Miller-Meeks"},{"y":2014,"o":"H","k":"IA-02","p":"R","v":129455,"s":47.36,"w":false,"n":"Mariannette Miller-Meeks"},{"y":2010,"o":"H","k":"IA-02","p":"R","v":104319,"s":45.92,"w":false,"n":"Mariannette Miller-Meeks"},{"y":2008,"o":"H","k":"IA-02","p":"R","v":118778,"s":38.8,"w":false,"n":"Mariannette Miller-Meeks"}]}